/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Take three consecutive supports A, B, C.
   - A₁, A₂ are the areas of the free bending moment diagrams of the two spans, in kN·m²; x̄₁, x̄₂ are the distances of their centroids from the outer supports A and C, in metres.
   - The right side is negative for downward loads.
   - The equation assumes the same EI along both spans, supports at one level with no settlement, and loads in the plane of the beam.
   - Two load cases cover most questions.
   - w₁, w₂ are the uniform loads in kN/m on the two spans.
   - For a central point load P₁ on L₁ and P₂ on L₂, it becomes
   - P₁, P₂ are the point loads in kN at midspan of the two spans.
   - Measure x̄₁ from A and x̄₂ from C, not from B.
*/
