/* book Worked example 2: Q: Change the beam of worked example 1 so that A is fixed; C stays a simple support. Spans 6 m and 4 m, w = 10 kN/m on both, constant EI. Find the support moments by moment distribution and check them with the three-moment equation.
   1. Stiffness at B: BA has a fixed far end, k = 4EI/6 = 0.667EI/m; BC has a pinned far end, k = 3EI/4 = 0.75EI/m. Σk = 1.417EI/m. DFBA = 0.471, DFBC = 0.529.
   2. Fixed end moments: AB fixed both ends, FEMAB = −wL²/12 = −30 kN·m, FEMBA = +30 kN·m; BC with C pinned, FEMBC = −wL²/8 = −20 kN·m.
   3. Joint B: unbalanced +30 − 20 = +10 kN·m. Balance −10: BA gets −4.71, BC gets −5.29 kN·m.
   4. Carry-over: half of −4.71 goes to A, −2.35 kN·m. Nothing goes to C (pinned). A is fixed, so it is never released; one cycle finishes the job.
   5. Final: MAB = −30 − 2.35 = −32.35 kN·m; MBA = 30 − 4.71 = +25.29; MBC = −20 − 5.29 = −25.29. Joint B sums to zero.
   6. Check by three moments with a zero-length span beyond A: 12MA + 6MB = −540 and 6MA + 20MB = −700 give MA = −32.35 and MB = −25.29 kN·m (hogging).
   Answer:  */
